+# v29 — four exact control exclusions, no padding
+
+Map panning and location selection now exclude only the four user-marked boxes:
+the Loong Haven title, legend, zoom/portrait area and bottom controls. The rest
+of the map content is available, including the right-side terrain between the
+legend and zoom slider. The old broad polygon and right strip are removed.
+There is no added padding around the boxes.
+
+Movement stops when the target's input pixel is available. Drag starts and
+intermediate cursor positions use the same four-box geometry. Reveal movements
+choose the nearest available pixel, rather than aiming at the old inner region.
+Window chrome and areas outside the captured game surface are not map content.
+
+A controlled Frontier Vault regression reproduces v28's reported stop on the
+second visit: a two-pixel viewport shift sends the target into the old right
+strip and provokes an ineffective tiny drag. v29 selects both visits directly.
+A two-pass atlas test also repeats the complete default route while preserving
+navigation between passes. These checks do not establish the exact state of
+the user's live game when the original stop occurred.
+
+Fast held movement, stationary release, fresh-frame checks, F10, saved routes,
+point removal, gem detection and inspection settings are retained.
+
+Close the old app, extract the full folder and run its LoongLens.exe. Settings,
+routes, screenshots and history remain in %LOCALAPPDATA%\LoongLens.
